<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3309" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκόν-η</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], ἡ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>whetstone, hone</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιθίνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Chilo
					1
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hermipp.
				46
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόξαν ἔχω ἀκόνας λιγυρᾶς ἐπὶ
				γλώσσᾳ</span> I feel the shrill note of a
			<i>whetstone</i> on my tongue, i.e. am roused to song, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				6.82
			</span></i>; of persons, e.g. a trainer, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδράσιν ἀεθληταῖσιν Ναξίαν ἀκόναν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>I.</u>
					6(5).73
				</span></i>
			; of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἔρως</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				12.18
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Alph.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.838e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> part of tragus
			of ear, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.86
			</span></i>. (Cf.Skt. <i>áśan</i>-
		'stone'.)</div>
